From fba1bcd1f5bbb91bd86773e7479c40a8da8bcc8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:54:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] agentHost: expose the Claude replay attribution index

Restoring a Claude session replays the transcript through ReplayBuilder,
which already indexes every tool_use by id (announcing turn, name, client
tool flag, parsed input) and then discards that index in finish(). The
only thing kept was SubagentRegistry.primeFromTranscript, which recovers
(toolCallId, agentId) pairs from completed Task results alone, so pending
spawns and every other tool use were lost on restore.

This is the pure foundation for hydrating a restored session's live
attribution state; no call site hydrates a live session yet.

replaySessionMessages now returns the turns together with the attribution
index (entries keyed by tool_use_id plus the tail turn id). Each entry
records whether its result was seen and, for Task/Agent spawns, the
agentId suffix the SDK wrote into the result. mapSessionMessagesToTurns
is a thin wrapper over it, so its callers are unchanged.

claudeAttributionResolver partitions that index into pending (unresolved
in the tail turn), dead (unresolved in an earlier turn, so no result can
ever arrive) and spawns. hydrateAttribution seeds ClaudeToolCallRegistry
through a new hydrate method that reuses the begin and _writeInfo paths
so display info matches the live path, marks each entry restored, and
records every spawn in SubagentRegistry.

The one behaviour change: primeFromTranscript now also records pending
Task/Agent parts (no agentId yet), matching what hydrateAttribution does,
so switching the restore path over later is behaviour neutral.
