From 4cca9568a8da5a304ed807ee11b639baa68ac1c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:29:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] agentHost: retain steer-preempted replay tool_uses as
 pending

Two review points on the replay attribution index, both correct.

buildAttributionSeed classified any unresolved tool_use outside the tail
turn as dead. That is wrong during a steer preempt: the steer input is
persisted as a later user envelope while a tool from the preempted request
can still return afterward (the case #334008 fixes). The replay data has no
reliable way to tell a steer folded into the running request from a genuine
later turn (M10: steering carries no Turn.id and no dependable isMeta
marker), so it now retains every unresolved entry as pending and never
drops one that might still receive a result. The dead bucket stays in the
seed shape, reserved for a future steer-aware transcript.

primeFromTranscript is reverted to its origin/main form so this PR is
genuinely foundation-only (option a). Recording pending spawns there was
not behaviour-neutral: _reconstructTurns calls it with the live session
registry, so a pending spawn would immediately make later inner envelopes
emit subagent_started through tagWithParent. That recording belongs to the
later hydration PR. hydrateAttribution still records pending spawns, but
nothing calls it on a live session in this PR.
